TC08 - Verify Language Tab Switching in Code Examples

Test Steps
Step	Action	Expected Result
1	Open https://playwright.dev/docs/intro	Installation documentation page is displayed successfully.
2	Locate the language selector tabs above a code block (e.g., "Node.js", "Python", "Java", ".NET").	Language tabs are visible above the code sample.
3	Verify "Node.js" is selected by default.	Node.js tab is highlighted/active and its code sample is shown.
4	Click the "Python" language tab.	The code sample updates to display Python-specific installation commands.
5	Verify the displayed command reflects Python syntax (e.g., "pip install playwright").	Python installation command is visible in the code block.
6	Scroll to another code block further down the page.	Additional code block is visible.
7	Verify the language selection ("Python") is remembered/synced across other code blocks on the page.	Other code blocks also display Python examples without needing re-selection.

Expected Final Result
The user can switch the programming language tab for code samples, the displayed commands update accordingly, and the language preference is consistently applied across multiple code blocks on the page.